[{"en":"Constantinople","fr":"Constantinople","de":"Konstantinopel","w":"Istanbul","wz":"伊斯坦布尔","coord":[28.98,41.01],"cap":[[330,1922]],"names":[{"from":-700,"to":329,"zh":"拜占庭","en":"Byzantion","loc":"Βυζάντιον"},{"from":330,"to":1452,"zh":"君士坦丁堡","en":"Constantinople","loc":"Κωνσταντινούπολις"},{"from":1453,"to":1929,"zh":"君士坦丁堡","en":"Constantinople","loc":"قسطنطينيه"},{"from":1930,"to":3000,"zh":"伊斯坦布尔","en":"Istanbul","loc":"İstanbul"}],"es":"Constantinopla","tag":{"zh":"两海之间 · 千年帝都","en":"City between two seas · capital for a millennium"},"desc":{"zh":"扼博斯普鲁斯海峡，控黑海与地中海之间、欧亚之间的通道。330年君士坦丁建都，此后为东罗马千年之都，1453年落入奥斯曼后又为伊斯兰世界的中心四百七十年。圣索菲亚大教堂与蓝色清真寺隔广场相望。","en":"Commands the Bosporus and the passage between the Black Sea and the Mediterranean, Europe and Asia. Constantine's capital from 330 and seat of the Eastern empire for a thousand years; after 1453 the Ottoman centre for 470 more. Hagia Sophia and the Blue Mosque face each other across a square."}},{"en":"Rome","fr":"Rome","de":"Rom","w":"Rome","wz":"罗马","coord":[12.49,41.89],"cap":[[-509,476],[756,1870],[1871,3000]],"names":[{"from":-753,"to":3000,"zh":"罗马","en":"Rome","loc":"Roma"}],"es":"Roma","tag":{"zh":"七丘之城 · 永恒之城","en":"City of seven hills · the Eternal City"},"desc":{"zh":"台伯河畔的城邦扩张为环地中海的帝国，前1世纪人口逾百万，是工业革命前欧洲唯一的百万城市。帝国衰落后由教宗统治，文艺复兴时再度成为艺术之都，1871年成为意大利首都。","en":"A city-state on the Tiber that grew into an empire ringing the Mediterranean; over a million people in the first century BCE, the only European city of that size before the industrial age. Papal after the empire, capital of Renaissance art, capital of Italy from 1871."}},{"en":"Alexandria","fr":"Alexandrie","de":"Alexandria","w":"Alexandria","wz":"亚历山大港","coord":[29.92,31.2],"cap":[[-305,-30]],"names":[{"from":-331,"to":640,"zh":"亚历山大里亚","en":"Alexandria","loc":"Ἀλεξάνδρεια"},{"from":641,"to":3000,"zh":"亚历山大","en":"Alexandria","loc":"الإسكندرية"}],"es":"Alejandría","tag":{"zh":"灯塔与图书馆","en":"Lighthouse and library"},"desc":{"zh":"前331年亚历山大所建，托勒密王朝之都。缪斯宫与大图书馆汇集希腊化世界的学问：欧几里得、埃拉托色尼、托勒密皆在此工作。法罗斯灯塔为古代七大奇迹之一。641年归阿拉伯后地位让予开罗。","en":"Founded by Alexander in 331 BCE and capital of the Ptolemies. The Museum and Library gathered the learning of the Hellenistic world: Euclid, Eratosthenes and Ptolemy worked here. The Pharos was one of the Seven Wonders. After the Arab conquest of 641 it yielded to Cairo."}},{"en":"Jerusalem","fr":"Jérusalem","de":"Jerusalem","w":"Jerusalem","wz":"耶路撒冷","coord":[35.22,31.78],"cap":[[1099,1187]],"names":[{"from":-1000,"to":134,"zh":"耶路撒冷","en":"Jerusalem","loc":"ירושלים"},{"from":135,"to":637,"zh":"埃利亚","en":"Aelia Capitolina","loc":"Aelia Capitolina"},{"from":638,"to":3000,"zh":"耶路撒冷","en":"Jerusalem","loc":"القدس"}],"es":"Jerusalén","tag":{"zh":"三教圣城","en":"Holy to three faiths"},"desc":{"zh":"大卫王之都，所罗门建圣殿，巴比伦与罗马两次毁之。耶稣在此受难，穆罕默德夜行登霄于此。十字军与萨拉丁反复争夺，奥斯曼统治四百年，今为以色列与巴勒斯坦争议之核心。","en":"David's capital, Solomon's Temple, twice destroyed by Babylon and Rome. Jesus was crucified here; Muhammad's night journey rose from here. Fought over by Crusaders and Saladin, Ottoman for four centuries, and the core of the Israeli-Palestinian dispute today."}},{"en":"Baghdad","fr":"Bagdad","de":"Bagdad","w":"Baghdad","wz":"巴格达","coord":[44.37,33.34],"cap":[[762,1258]],"names":[{"from":762,"to":3000,"zh":"巴格达","en":"Baghdad","loc":"بغداد"}],"es":"Bagdad","tag":{"zh":"圆城 · 智慧宫","en":"The Round City · House of Wisdom"},"desc":{"zh":"762年哈里发曼苏尔在底格里斯河畔建圆城，阿拔斯王朝五百年之都。9世纪智慧宫翻译希腊、波斯、印度典籍，人口逾百万，是当时世界最大城市。1258年旭烈兀屠城，巴格达再未恢复此等地位。","en":"Caliph al-Mansur's round city on the Tigris, founded 762 and Abbasid capital for five centuries. The ninth-century House of Wisdom translated Greek, Persian and Indian learning; with over a million people it was the world's largest city. Hulagu's sack of 1258 ended that era for good."}},{"en":"Damascus","fr":"Damas","de":"Damaskus","w":"Damascus","wz":"大马士革","coord":[36.29,33.51],"cap":[[661,750]],"names":[{"from":-1000,"to":3000,"zh":"大马士革","en":"Damascus","loc":"دمشق"}],"es":"Damasco","tag":{"zh":"最古老的持续有人居住的城市","en":"Oldest continuously inhabited city"},"desc":{"zh":"有人定居逾四千年。倭马亚王朝之都（661–750），倭马亚大清真寺建于拜占庭教堂之上。保罗在此皈信，萨拉丁葬于此。奥斯曼时为朝觐商队的集结地。","en":"Settled for over four thousand years. Umayyad capital 661–750; the Great Mosque rose on a Byzantine church. Paul was converted here and Saladin is buried here. Under the Ottomans the gathering point for the pilgrim caravan."}},{"en":"Cordoba","fr":"Cordoue","de":"Córdoba","w":"Córdoba, Spain","wz":"科尔多瓦 (西班牙)","coord":[-4.78,37.88],"cap":[[756,1031]],"names":[{"from":-200,"to":710,"zh":"科尔杜巴","en":"Corduba","loc":"Corduba"},{"from":711,"to":1235,"zh":"科尔多瓦","en":"Córdoba","loc":"قرطبة"},{"from":1236,"to":3000,"zh":"科尔多瓦","en":"Córdoba","loc":"Córdoba"}],"es":"Córdoba","tag":{"zh":"西方的巴格达","en":"Baghdad of the West"},"desc":{"zh":"756年倭马亚流亡者在此建埃米尔国，929年称哈里发。10世纪人口近五十万，图书馆藏书四十万卷，犹太、基督、穆斯林学者共处；大清真寺的八百根柱子是伊斯兰西班牙的象征。1236年卡斯蒂利亚收复。","en":"An Umayyad exile founded the emirate here in 756; caliphate from 929. In the tenth century nearly half a million people, a library of 400,000 volumes, Jewish, Christian and Muslim scholars side by side; the Great Mosque's forest of columns is the emblem of Islamic Spain. Taken by Castile in 1236."}},{"en":"Paris","fr":"Paris","de":"Paris","w":"Paris","wz":"巴黎","coord":[2.35,48.86],"cap":[[987,3000]],"names":[{"from":-52,"to":359,"zh":"卢泰西亚","en":"Lutetia","loc":"Lutetia"},{"from":360,"to":3000,"zh":"巴黎","en":"Paris","loc":"Paris"}],"es":"París","tag":{"zh":"塞纳河上的岛 · 大学与革命","en":"Island on the Seine · university and revolution"},"desc":{"zh":"高卢部落的河心岛寨，罗马的卢泰西亚，987年卡佩王朝定都。12世纪巴黎大学成为欧洲神学与哲学中心，圣母院动工；1789年从此点燃革命；19世纪奥斯曼改造成林荫大道之城，印象派与现代艺术在此诞生。","en":"A Gaulish island stronghold, Roman Lutetia, Capetian capital from 987. In the twelfth century its university led European theology and Notre-Dame was begun; in 1789 revolution broke out here; Haussmann's boulevards in the nineteenth century, and the birth of Impressionism and modern art."}},{"en":"London","fr":"Londres","de":"London","w":"London","wz":"伦敦","coord":[-0.13,51.51],"cap":[[1066,3000]],"names":[{"from":47,"to":410,"zh":"伦蒂尼恩","en":"Londinium","loc":"Londinium"},{"from":411,"to":3000,"zh":"伦敦","en":"London","loc":"London"}],"es":"Londres","tag":{"zh":"泰晤士河港 · 帝国之都","en":"Port on the Thames · imperial capital"},"desc":{"zh":"罗马人于公元47年建伦蒂尼恩，1066年后诺曼王朝之都。中世纪为羊毛贸易港，17世纪后金融城崛起，18–19世纪为世界最大城市与大英帝国的中枢，1851年万国博览会在此举行。","en":"Founded by Rome as Londinium in 47 CE, Norman capital after 1066. Medieval wool port, then the City's rise as a financial centre; in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries the world's largest city and the hub of the British Empire. The Great Exhibition of 1851 was held here."}},{"en":"Carthage","fr":"Carthage","de":"Karthago","w":"Carthage","wz":"迦太基","coord":[10.32,36.85],"cap":[[-814,-146]],"names":[{"from":-814,"to":698,"zh":"迦太基","en":"Carthage","loc":"Qart-ḥadašt"},{"from":699,"to":3000,"zh":"突尼斯","en":"Tunis","loc":"تونس"}],"es":"Cartago","tag":{"zh":"腓尼基殖民地 · 罗马的宿敌","en":"Phoenician colony · Rome's great rival"},"desc":{"zh":"前814年推罗人所建，前6世纪起控制西地中海贸易。三次布匿战争后前146年被罗马夷平、撒盐；后罗马重建为阿非利加行省首府，奥古斯丁在此求学。698年阿拉伯人毁之，突尼斯取而代之。","en":"Founded by Tyre in 814 BCE; master of western Mediterranean trade from the sixth century. Razed and salted by Rome in 146 BCE after three Punic Wars, rebuilt as capital of Africa province, where Augustine studied. Destroyed by the Arabs in 698 and replaced by Tunis."}},{"en":"Athens","fr":"Athènes","de":"Athen","w":"Athens","wz":"雅典","coord":[23.73,37.98],"cap":[[-508,-322],[1834,3000]],"names":[{"from":-1000,"to":3000,"zh":"雅典","en":"Athens","loc":"Ἀθῆναι"}],"es":"Atenas","tag":{"zh":"民主与哲学的发源地","en":"Cradle of democracy and philosophy"},"desc":{"zh":"前508年克里斯提尼改革立民主制，前5世纪伯里克利时代建帕特农神庙，苏格拉底、柏拉图、亚里士多德相继在此讲学。罗马时为大学城，529年查士丁尼关闭学园。奥斯曼统治近四百年，1834年成为希腊王国首都。","en":"Democracy from Cleisthenes' reforms of 508 BCE; the Parthenon under Pericles; Socrates, Plato and Aristotle taught here in turn. A university town under Rome until Justinian closed the Academy in 529. Ottoman for nearly four centuries, capital of Greece from 1834."}},{"en":"Antioch","fr":"Antioche","de":"Antiochia","w":"Antioch","wz":"安条克","coord":[36.16,36.2],"cap":[[-300,-64]],"names":[{"from":-300,"to":1268,"zh":"安条克","en":"Antioch","loc":"Ἀντιόχεια"},{"from":1269,"to":3000,"zh":"安塔基亚","en":"Antakya","loc":"Antakya"}],"es":"Antioquía","tag":{"zh":"奥龙特斯河上的大城","en":"Great city on the Orontes"},"desc":{"zh":"前300年塞琉古一世所建，塞琉古王国之都，罗马帝国第三大城。\"基督徒\"一词在此首次使用，保罗由此出发传教。六世纪地震与波斯劫掠后衰落，1098年十字军围城九月攻克。","en":"Founded by Seleucus I in 300 BCE, Seleucid capital and third city of the Roman empire. The word \"Christian\" was first used here, and Paul set out from here. Earthquakes and Persian sacks in the sixth century broke it; the First Crusade took it after a nine-month siege in 1098."}},{"en":"Cairo","fr":"Le Caire","de":"Kairo","w":"Cairo","wz":"开罗","coord":[31.24,30.05],"cap":[[969,3000]],"names":[{"from":641,"to":968,"zh":"福斯塔特","en":"Fustat","loc":"الفسطاط"},{"from":969,"to":3000,"zh":"开罗","en":"Cairo","loc":"القاهرة"}],"es":"El Cairo","tag":{"zh":"尼罗河畔的胜利之城","en":"City of victory on the Nile"},"desc":{"zh":"641年阿拉伯人建福斯塔特，969年法蒂玛王朝建开罗（\"胜利者\"），爱资哈尔清真寺与大学同时创立。马穆鲁克时期为伊斯兰世界第一大城，伊本·白图泰称之为\"城市之母\"。吉萨金字塔在其西郊。","en":"The Arabs founded Fustat in 641; the Fatimids built al-Qahira, \"the Victorious\", in 969, with al-Azhar mosque and university. Under the Mamluks the largest city in Islam; Ibn Battuta called it the mother of cities. The pyramids of Giza stand on its western edge."}},{"en":"Samarkand","fr":"Samarcande","de":"Samarkand","w":"Samarkand","wz":"撒马尔罕","coord":[66.97,39.65],"cap":[[1370,1405]],"names":[{"from":-700,"to":710,"zh":"马拉坎达 / 康国","en":"Maracanda","loc":"Μαράκανδα"},{"from":711,"to":3000,"zh":"撒马尔罕","en":"Samarkand","loc":"سمرقند"}],"es":"Samarcanda","tag":{"zh":"丝路之心 · 帖木儿之都","en":"Heart of the Silk Road · Timur's capital"},"desc":{"zh":"粟特人的马拉坎达，前329年亚历山大攻取，唐代为康国。8世纪阿拉伯人在此学会造纸，1220年成吉思汗屠城，1370年帖木儿重建为帝都，雷吉斯坦广场与比比哈努姆清真寺为中亚建筑之冠。兀鲁伯在此建天文台。","en":"Sogdian Maracanda, taken by Alexander in 329 BCE, Kang to the Tang. Here the Arabs learned papermaking in the eighth century; Genghis sacked it in 1220; Timur rebuilt it as his capital from 1370, with the Registan and Bibi-Khanym mosque. Ulugh Beg built his observatory here."}},{"en":"Kyiv","fr":"Kiev","de":"Kiew","w":"Kyiv","wz":"基辅","coord":[30.52,50.45],"cap":[[882,1240]],"names":[{"from":880,"to":3000,"zh":"基辅","en":"Kyiv","loc":"Київ"}],"es":"Kiev","tag":{"zh":"罗斯诸城之母","en":"Mother of Rus' cities"},"desc":{"zh":"第聂伯河畔的瓦良格贸易站，882年起为基辅罗斯之都。988年弗拉基米尔受洗，东斯拉夫人皈依东正教；圣索菲亚大教堂仿君士坦丁堡而建。1240年蒙古屠城后衰落，俄罗斯与乌克兰皆以此为历史源头。","en":"A Varangian trading post on the Dnieper, capital of Kievan Rus' from 882. Vladimir's baptism in 988 brought the East Slavs into Orthodoxy; St Sophia copied Constantinople's. Sacked by the Mongols in 1240; both Russia and Ukraine trace their origins here."}},{"en":"Moscow","fr":"Moscou","de":"Moskau","w":"Moscow","wz":"莫斯科","coord":[37.62,55.75],"cap":[[1283,1712],[1918,3000]],"names":[{"from":1147,"to":3000,"zh":"莫斯科","en":"Moscow","loc":"Москва"}],"es":"Moscú","tag":{"zh":"第三罗马","en":"The Third Rome"},"desc":{"zh":"1147年首见记载的边地小镇，蒙古统治下作为征税代理人崛起，1480年摆脱金帐汗国。伊凡三世娶拜占庭末代公主，自称\"第三罗马\"；1712年彼得迁都圣彼得堡，1918年苏维埃政权迁回。","en":"A frontier town first recorded in 1147 that rose as the Mongols' tax collector and threw off the Golden Horde in 1480. Ivan III married the last Byzantine princess and claimed the title of Third Rome; Peter moved the capital to St Petersburg in 1712, the Soviets moved it back in 1918."}},{"en":"Venice","fr":"Venise","de":"Venedig","w":"Venice","wz":"威尼斯","coord":[12.34,45.44],"cap":[[697,1797]],"names":[{"from":697,"to":3000,"zh":"威尼斯","en":"Venice","loc":"Venezia"}],"es":"Venecia","tag":{"zh":"最宁静的共和国","en":"La Serenissima"},"desc":{"zh":"蛮族入侵时避入潟湖的难民所建，697年起由总督统治，名义上属拜占庭。1204年主导第四次十字军洗劫君士坦丁堡，获得东地中海贸易霸权；马可·波罗由此东行。1797年拿破仑终结其一千一百年的共和。","en":"Founded by refugees in the lagoon during the barbarian invasions, ruled by doges from 697, nominally Byzantine. Engineered the Fourth Crusade's sack of Constantinople in 1204 and won dominance of eastern Mediterranean trade; Marco Polo sailed from here. Napoleon ended its eleven-hundred-year republic in 1797."}},{"en":"Babylon","fr":"Babylone","de":"Babylon","w":"Babylon","wz":"巴比伦","coord":[44.42,32.54],"cap":[[-1894,-539]],"names":[{"from":-2000,"to":-141,"zh":"巴比伦","en":"Babylon","loc":"Bābilim"}],"es":"Babilonia","tag":{"zh":"两河的门 · 空中花园","en":"Gate of the gods · the Hanging Gardens"},"desc":{"zh":"汉谟拉比之都，尼布甲尼撒二世时为世界最大城市，伊什塔尔门与空中花园闻名。前539年居鲁士入城，前331年亚历山大入城并死于此。塞琉西亚建成后逐渐废弃。","en":"Hammurabi's capital; under Nebuchadnezzar II the largest city in the world, with the Ishtar Gate and the Hanging Gardens. Cyrus entered it in 539 BCE, Alexander in 331 and died here. It faded after Seleucia was built nearby."}},{"en":"Persepolis","fr":"Persépolis","de":"Persepolis","w":"Persepolis","wz":"波斯波利斯","coord":[52.89,29.93],"cap":[[-515,-330]],"names":[{"from":-515,"to":-330,"zh":"波斯波利斯","en":"Persepolis","loc":"Pārsa"}],"es":"Persépolis","tag":{"zh":"波斯诸王之城","en":"City of the Persian kings"},"desc":{"zh":"大流士一世前515年始建，阿契美尼德王朝举行新年朝贡典礼之地，浮雕刻画二十三个属国使节献礼。前330年亚历山大焚其宫殿，此后再未重建。","en":"Begun by Darius I in 515 BCE for the Achaemenid New Year tribute ceremonies; its reliefs show envoys of twenty-three subject nations bearing gifts. Alexander burned the palaces in 330 BCE and it was never rebuilt."}},{"en":"Mecca","fr":"La Mecque","de":"Mekka","w":"Mecca","wz":"麦加","coord":[39.83,21.42],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":0,"to":3000,"zh":"麦加","en":"Mecca","loc":"مكة"}],"es":"La Meca","tag":{"zh":"天房所在","en":"City of the Kaaba"},"desc":{"zh":"阿拉伯半岛西部的商队城市，天房在伊斯兰教之前已是朝圣地。穆罕默德生于此，622年出走麦地那，630年收复。此后十四个世纪，全球穆斯林每日朝向此地礼拜，每年朝觐。","en":"A caravan city of western Arabia whose Kaaba was a pilgrimage shrine before Islam. Muhammad was born here, left for Medina in 622 and returned in 630. For fourteen centuries since, Muslims everywhere have faced it in prayer and come on the hajj."}},{"en":"Vienna","fr":"Vienne","de":"Wien","w":"Vienna","wz":"维也纳","coord":[16.37,48.21],"cap":[[1440,3000]],"names":[{"from":0,"to":3000,"zh":"维也纳","en":"Vienna","loc":"Wien"}],"es":"Viena","tag":{"zh":"哈布斯堡的首都 · 奥斯曼的止步处","en":"Habsburg capital · where the Ottomans stopped"},"desc":{"zh":"罗马军营文多波纳，1440年起为哈布斯堡王朝之都。1529与1683年两次击退奥斯曼围城。18–19世纪为海顿、莫扎特、贝多芬、舒伯特之城，1815年维也纳会议重划欧洲；世纪末有弗洛伊德、克里姆特与维也纳学派。","en":"Roman Vindobona, Habsburg seat from 1440. Twice repelled Ottoman sieges, in 1529 and 1683. The city of Haydn, Mozart, Beethoven and Schubert; the Congress of 1815 redrew Europe here; at the century's end, Freud, Klimt and the Vienna Circle."}},{"en":"Berlin","fr":"Berlin","de":"Berlin","w":"Berlin","wz":"柏林","coord":[13.4,52.52],"cap":[[1701,3000]],"names":[{"from":1237,"to":3000,"zh":"柏林","en":"Berlin","loc":"Berlin"}],"es":"Berlín"},{"en":"Amsterdam","fr":"Amsterdam","de":"Amsterdam","w":"Amsterdam","wz":"阿姆斯特丹","coord":[4.9,52.37],"cap":[[1588,3000]],"names":[{"from":1275,"to":3000,"zh":"阿姆斯特丹","en":"Amsterdam","loc":"Amsterdam"}],"es":"Ámsterdam"},{"en":"St Petersburg","fr":"Saint-Pétersbourg","de":"Sankt Petersburg","w":"Saint Petersburg","wz":"圣彼得堡","coord":[30.32,59.93],"cap":[[1712,1917]],"names":[{"from":1703,"to":1913,"zh":"圣彼得堡","en":"St Petersburg","loc":"Санкт-Петербург"},{"from":1914,"to":1923,"zh":"彼得格勒","en":"Petrograd","loc":"Петроград"},{"from":1924,"to":1990,"zh":"列宁格勒","en":"Leningrad","loc":"Ленинград"},{"from":1991,"to":3000,"zh":"圣彼得堡","en":"St Petersburg","loc":"Санкт-Петербург"}],"es":"San Petersburgo","tag":{"zh":"通往欧洲的窗户","en":"Window on Europe"},"desc":{"zh":"1703年彼得大帝在涅瓦河口沼泽上建城，1712年定都，意大利与法国建筑师设计的巴洛克与新古典主义之城。1825年十二月党人起义、1905年血腥星期日、1917年二月与十月革命均发生于此。","en":"Founded by Peter the Great on the Neva marshes in 1703, capital from 1712, laid out by Italian and French architects in Baroque and Neoclassical style. The Decembrist rising of 1825, Bloody Sunday of 1905 and the February and October revolutions of 1917 all happened here."}},{"en":"Isfahan","fr":"Ispahan","de":"Isfahan","w":"Isfahan","wz":"伊斯法罕","coord":[51.68,32.65],"cap":[[1598,1736]],"names":[{"from":0,"to":3000,"zh":"伊斯法罕","en":"Isfahan","loc":"اصفهان"}],"es":"Isfahán","tag":{"zh":"伊斯法罕半天下","en":"Isfahan is half the world"},"desc":{"zh":"塞尔柱与萨法维两朝之都。1598年阿拔斯一世迁都于此，建王侯广场、皇家清真寺与三十三孔桥，人口六十万，欧洲使节与亚美尼亚商人云集；波斯谚语称\"伊斯法罕半天下\"。","en":"Capital of the Seljuks and the Safavids. Abbas I moved his court here in 1598 and built the Royal Square, the Shah Mosque and the bridge of thirty-three arches; 600,000 people, European envoys and Armenian merchants. \"Isfahan is half the world\", ran the Persian saying."}},{"en":"Lisbon","fr":"Lisbonne","de":"Lissabon","w":"Lisbon","wz":"里斯本","coord":[-9.14,38.72],"cap":[[1256,3000]],"names":[{"from":-1200,"to":3000,"zh":"里斯本","en":"Lisbon","loc":"Lisboa"}],"es":"Lisboa"},{"en":"Madrid","fr":"Madrid","de":"Madrid","w":"Madrid","wz":"马德里","coord":[-3.7,40.42],"cap":[[1561,3000]],"names":[{"from":860,"to":3000,"zh":"马德里","en":"Madrid","loc":"Madrid"}]},{"en":"Toledo","fr":"Tolède","de":"Toledo","w":"Toledo, Spain","wz":"托莱多","coord":[-4.02,39.86],"cap":[[542,711],[1085,1561]],"names":[{"from":-200,"to":3000,"zh":"托莱多","en":"Toledo","loc":"Toledo"}],"es":"Toledo"},{"en":"Seville","fr":"Séville","de":"Sevilla","w":"Seville","wz":"塞维利亚","coord":[-5.99,37.39],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":-800,"to":3000,"zh":"塞维利亚","en":"Seville","loc":"Sevilla"}],"es":"Sevilla"},{"en":"Marseille","fr":"Marseille","de":"Marseille","w":"Marseille","wz":"马赛","coord":[5.37,43.3],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":-600,"to":3000,"zh":"马赛","en":"Marseille","loc":"Marseille"}],"es":"Marsella"},{"en":"Lyon","fr":"Lyon","de":"Lyon","w":"Lyon","wz":"里昂","coord":[4.84,45.76],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":-43,"to":3000,"zh":"里昂","en":"Lyon","loc":"Lyon"}],"es":"Lyon"},{"en":"Aachen","fr":"Aix-la-Chapelle","de":"Aachen","w":"Aachen","wz":"亚琛","coord":[6.08,50.78],"cap":[[794,814]],"names":[{"from":100,"to":3000,"zh":"亚琛","en":"Aachen","loc":"Aachen"}],"es":"Aquisgrán"},{"en":"Cologne","fr":"Cologne","de":"