 century to 1920. The Samanid mausoleum is Central Asia's oldest Islamic building."}},{"en":"Merv","fr":"Merv","de":"Merw","w":"Merv","wz":"木鹿","coord":[62.19,37.66],"cap":[[1118,1157]],"names":[{"from":-600,"to":3000,"zh":"木鹿","en":"Merv","loc":"مرو"}]},{"en":"Balkh","fr":"Balkh","de":"Balch","w":"Balkh","wz":"巴尔赫","coord":[66.9,36.76],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":-1000,"to":3000,"zh":"巴尔赫","en":"Balkh","loc":"بلخ"}]},{"en":"Herat","fr":"Hérat","de":"Herat","w":"Herat","wz":"赫拉特","coord":[62.2,34.34],"cap":[[1405,1507]],"names":[{"from":-500,"to":3000,"zh":"赫拉特","en":"Herat","loc":"هرات"}],"es":"Herat"},{"en":"Kabul","fr":"Kaboul","de":"Kabul","w":"Kabul","wz":"喀布尔","coord":[69.17,34.53],"cap":[[1504,1526],[1776,3000]],"names":[{"from":-1500,"to":3000,"zh":"喀布尔","en":"Kabul","loc":"کابل"}],"es":"Kabul"},{"en":"Kashgar","fr":"Kachgar","de":"Kaschgar","w":"Kashgar","wz":"喀什市","coord":[75.99,39.47],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":-200,"to":3000,"zh":"喀什","en":"Kashgar","loc":"قەشقەر"}],"es":"Kasgar"},{"en":"Dunhuang","fr":"Dunhuang","de":"Dunhuang","w":"Dunhuang","wz":"敦煌市","coord":[94.66,40.14],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":-111,"to":3000,"zh":"敦煌","en":"Dunhuang","loc":"敦煌"}]},{"en":"Chang'an","fr":"Chang'an","de":"Chang'an","w":"Chang'an","wz":"长安","coord":[108.94,34.26],"cap":[[-202,8],[618,904]],"names":[{"from":-1046,"to":3000,"zh":"长安","en":"Chang'an","loc":"长安"}],"es":"Chang'an","tag":{"zh":"丝路起点 · 唐之都","en":"Head of the Silk Road · Tang capital"},"desc":{"zh":"西周丰镐、秦咸阳皆在近旁，汉与唐建都于此。唐长安城八十四平方公里，人口百万，为当时世界最大城市，波斯、粟特、日本、新罗人杂处，佛寺、景教寺、祆祠并立。904年毁于战乱，后为西安。","en":"Near the Zhou and Qin capitals; seat of the Han and the Tang. Tang Chang'an covered 84 square kilometres with a million people, the largest city on earth, where Persians, Sogdians, Japanese and Koreans mixed and Buddhist, Nestorian and Zoroastrian temples stood together. Destroyed in 904; later Xi'an."}},{"en":"Luoyang","fr":"Luoyang","de":"Luoyang","w":"Luoyang","wz":"洛阳市","coord":[112.45,34.62],"cap":[[25,190],[493,534]],"names":[{"from":-1600,"to":3000,"zh":"洛阳","en":"Luoyang","loc":"洛阳"}]},{"en":"Kaifeng","fr":"Kaifeng","de":"Kaifeng","w":"Kaifeng","wz":"开封市","coord":[114.3,34.8],"cap":[[960,1127]],"names":[{"from":-364,"to":3000,"zh":"开封","en":"Kaifeng","loc":"开封"}]},{"en":"Hangzhou","fr":"Hangzhou","de":"Hangzhou","w":"Hangzhou","wz":"杭州市","coord":[120.17,30.27],"cap":[[1138,1276]],"names":[{"from":-221,"to":3000,"zh":"杭州","en":"Hangzhou","loc":"杭州"}]},{"en":"Beijing","fr":"Pékin","de":"Peking","w":"Beijing","wz":"北京市","coord":[116.4,39.9],"cap":[[1272,1368],[1421,3000]],"names":[{"from":-1045,"to":3000,"zh":"北京","en":"Beijing","loc":"北京"}],"es":"Pekín","tag":{"zh":"六朝古都","en":"Capital of six dynasties"},"desc":{"zh":"战国燕都蓟，辽为南京，金为中都，1272年忽必烈建大都为元之都，1421年永乐迁都于此建紫禁城。明清两代为中国首都五百年，1949年起为中华人民共和国首都。","en":"Ji of the Warring States Yan, Southern Capital of the Liao, Zhongdu of the Jin; Kublai built Dadu here in 1272, and Yongle moved the Ming court here in 1421 and built the Forbidden City. Chinese capital for five centuries under Ming and Qing, and since 1949."}},{"en":"Nanjing","fr":"Nankin","de":"Nanking","w":"Nanjing","wz":"南京市","coord":[118.8,32.06],"cap":[[229,589],[1368,1421]],"names":[{"from":-472,"to":3000,"zh":"南京","en":"Nanjing","loc":"南京"}],"es":"Nankín"},{"en":"Guangzhou","fr":"Canton","de":"Guangzhou","w":"Guangzhou","wz":"广州市","coord":[113.26,23.13],"cap":[],"names":[{"from":-214,"to":3000,"zh":"广州","en":"Guangzhou","loc":"广州"}],"es":"Cantón"},{"en":"Lhasa","fr":"Lhassa","de":"Lhasa","w":"Lhasa","wz":"拉萨市","coord":[91.12,29.65],"cap":[[633,842],[1642,1959]],"names":[{"from":633,"to":3000,"zh":"拉萨","en":"Lhasa","loc":"ལྷ་ས་"}],"es":"Lhasa"},{"en":"Kyoto","fr":"Kyoto","de":"Kyōto","w":"Kyoto","wz":"京都市","coord":[135.77,35.01],"cap":[[794,1868]],"names":[{"from":794,"to":3000,"zh":"京都","en":"Kyoto","loc":"京都"}],"es":"Kioto","tag":{"zh":"平安京","en":"Heian-kyō"},"desc":{"zh":"794年桓武天皇仿长安建都，为日本首都一千零七十四年。平安时代的宫廷文化产生《源氏物语》；镰仓、室町以降天皇居此而幕府在别处；1868年明治迁都东京。","en":"Modelled on Chang'an by Emperor Kanmu in 794 and capital of Japan for 1,074 years. Heian court culture produced the Tale of Genji; under the shogunates the emperor stayed here while power sat elsewhere; the Meiji court moved to Tokyo in 1868."}},{"en":"Kamakura","fr":"Kamakura","de":"Kamakura","w":"Kamakura","wz":"镰仓市","coord":[139.55,35.32],"cap":[[1185,1333]],"names":[{"from":1180,"to":3000,"zh":"镰仓","en":"Kamakura","loc":"鎌倉"}]},{"en":"Edo","fr":"Edo","de":"Edo","w":"Tokyo","wz":"东京","coord":[139.69,35.69],"cap":[[1603,3000]],"names":[{"from":1457,"to":3000,"zh":"江户","en":"Edo","loc":"江戸"}],"es":"Edo"},{"en":"Gyeongju","fr":"Gyeongju","de":"Gyeongju","w":"Gyeongju","wz":"庆州市","coord":[129.22,35.84],"cap":[[-57,935]],"names":[{"from":-57,"to":3000,"zh":"庆州","en":"Gyeongju","loc":"경주"}]},{"en":"Hanyang","fr":"Hanyang","de":"Hanyang","w":"Seoul","wz":"首尔","coord":[126.98,37.57],"cap":[[1394,3000]],"names":[{"from":18,"to":3000,"zh":"汉阳","en":"Hanyang","loc":"한양"}],"es":"Seúl"},{"en":"Delhi","fr":"Delhi","de":"Delhi","w":"Delhi","wz":"德里","coord":[77.21,28.61],"cap":[[1206,1526],[1648,1857],[1911,3000]],"names":[{"from":736,"to":3000,"zh":"德里","en":"Delhi","loc":"दिल्ली"}],"es":"Delhi","tag":{"zh":"七座城市的遗址","en":"Site of seven cities"},"desc":{"zh":"1206年起为德里苏丹国之都，库特布塔见证伊斯兰统治的开端；1398年帖木儿屠城。莫卧儿沙贾汗1648年建新城沙贾汉纳巴德（旧德里），1911年英国自加尔各答迁都于此，1931年新德里落成。","en":"Capital of the Delhi Sultanate from 1206; the Qutb Minar marks the start of Muslim rule; Timur sacked it in 1398. Shah Jahan built Shahjahanabad (Old Delhi) in 1648; the British moved their capital here from Calcutta in 1911 and inaugurated New Delhi in 1931."}},{"en":"Agra","fr":"Agra","de":"Agra","w":"Agra","wz":"阿格拉","coord":[78.01,27.18],"cap":[[1526,1648]],"names":[{"from":1504,"to":3000,"zh":"阿格拉","en":"Agra","loc":"आगरा"}]},{"en":"Pataliputra","fr":"Pataliputra","de":"Pataliputra","w":"Pataliputra","wz":"华氏城","coord":[85.14,25.61],"cap":[[-321,-185],[320,550]],"names":[{"from":-490,"to":3000,"zh":"华氏城","en":"Pataliputra","loc":